Usage: numfmt [OPTION]... [NUMBER]...

Convert numbers from/to human-readable strings.
Convert numbers to/from human-readable strings (e.g., 1K, 1M).
If no number is specified, read from standard input.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --delimiter ARG       use X instead of whitespace for field delimiter
      --from ARG            autoconvert from X
      --to ARG              autoconvert to X
      --round ARG           use METHOD for rounding
      --padding NUM         pad numbers to width N
      --pad NUM             pad numbers to width N
      --suffix ARG          add STRING after formatted numbers
      --field ARG           replace the numbers in these input fields
  -f, --format ARG          use printf style floating-point FORMAT
      --header[=NUM]        print the first N header lines unchanged
      --grouping            group digits with locale thousands separator
      --invalid ARG         set policy for invalid values: 'abort' (default),
                            'warn', 'ignore'
      --debug               print conversion diagnostics
      --from-unit ARG       multiply input numbers by UNIT
      --to-unit ARG         divide numbers by UNIT before formatting
      --unit-separator ARG  use STRING between number and unit
  -z, --zero-terminated     line delimiter is NUL, not newline
  -M                        use IEC units (powers of 1024)
  -l                        use locale grouping
      --help                display this help and exit
  -V, --version             output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
